Maintainer: Matteo Pelagatti <matteo.pelagatti@unimib.it>
Description: A set of functions to compute the Hodrick-Prescott (HP)
    filter and spline smoothing with automatically selected jumps. The original
    HP filter and spline smoothing extract a smooth signal, and our version
    allows for a small number of automatically identified jumps. Smoothing
    splines with discontinuities are obtained either by time warping, or by the
    dynamic-programming algorithm of Storath and Weinmann (2024)
    <doi:10.1080/10618600.2023.2262000>. See Pelagatti, Maranzano and Gatto
    Ronchieri (2026) <doi:10.48550/arXiv.2610.33137> for details on the
    smoothing splines with discontinuities, and Maranzano and Pelagatti (2025)
    <doi:10.1016/j.econmod.2025.107132> for details on the HP filter with
    jumps.
